                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Houston/Galveston TX",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 2 at 9:50PM CDT until September 3 at 7:00AM CDT by NWS Houston/Galveston TX",
                "description": "Flood Watch Still In Effect for Portions of Southeast Texas.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southeast Texas, including the following\nareas, Brazos, Coastal Harris, Grimes, Houston, Inland Harris,\nMadison, Montgomery, Northern Liberty, Polk, San Jacinto, Southern\nLiberty, Trinity, Walker and Waller.\n\n* WHEN...Until 7 AM CDT Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- A swath of 3 to 10 inches has fallen over portions of southeast\nTexas over the last 24 hours. Pockets of higher totals between\n10-15+ inches has been observed in Liberty and Polk counties. The\nremnants of Edouard have stalled over the Piney Woods which will\nlead to additional periods of moderate to heavy rainfall through\nThursday. An additional 2-6 inches with isolated higher totals of\n10-12 inches are possible over the next 24 hours. The NWS has\nissued a High Risk for excessive rainfall through Thursday\nmorning and potential flash flooding for the hardest hit areas\nespecially as rainfall rates will exceed 2-4 inches per hour.\nThose living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared to\ntake action should flooding develop. Stay weather aware and be\nready to take action when Flash Flood Warnings are issued,\nparticularly wireless emergency alert Flash Flood Warnings for\nconsiderable and/or catastrophic flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop especially at night.\n\nDo not drive your vehicle or walk into areas where water covers the\nroadway as the water depth may be too great to allow you to cross\nsafely.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
